# Unit Tests Required

All behavior changes must include unit test coverage in the same task.

## Requirements

- Update existing unit tests when changing behavior in existing code.
- Add new unit tests when introducing new behavior or branches.
- Do not merge code-only changes without corresponding test changes.
- Keep tests focused on user-visible behavior and critical integration points.

## Minimum Expectations

- If a component handler changes (create/update/delete flows), update its page test file.
- If confirmation or error flows change, include tests for both success and cancel/failure paths when applicable.
- If text/labels/messages change and are behavior-relevant, update assertions accordingly.

## Examples

```jsx
// ❌ WRONG: behavior changed, no test updates
const handleDelete = () => setConfirmDialog({ ... });
```

```jsx
// ✅ CORRECT: behavior changed + tests updated
await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /excluir/i }));
await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: /confirmar/i }));
expect(api.delete).toHaveBeenCalled();
```
